Third-Party Components and References
================================================================================

Sub-Store — DSL compatibility only, NO source code is used
----------------------------------------------------------
  Upstream:  https://github.com/sub-store-org/Sub-Store
  License:   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
  Authors:   Peng-YM and Sub-Store contributors

  SubPilot does NOT vendor, copy, or derive any source code from Sub-Store.
  Its server-side source (apps/server/src/) is an independent implementation
  written from scratch: it has no Sub-Store imports, no shared modules, no
  ported files, and no build-time path aliases pointing at Sub-Store.

  What it DOES share is a *user-facing convention*: the JSON operator chain
  uses the same operator type names for a few entries (for example
  "Flag Operator", "Sort Operator", "Useless Filter") and accepts Sub-Store's
  inline `(?i)` regex flag syntax. This is interface-level compatibility so
  that scripts written for Sub-Store's node-processing feature remain
  recognizable here. Several operator names were also deliberately renamed
  (e.g. "Regex Rename Operator" -> "Regex Rename"), which further shows this is
  an independent naming pass rather than a copy.

  The operator type names themselves are short functional labels and are used
  here under the terms of the AGPL-3.0, with credit to the Sub-Store project.

SubPilot-Archive — the predecessor project (archived, private)
--------------------------------------------------------------
  Upstream:  https://github.com/guanxi660-crypto/SubPilot-Archive
  License:   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0

  SubPilot-Archive is the earlier project by the same author, from which
  SubPilot inherits its UI conventions and one data file. It is itself a
  derivative work of Sub-Store (its own NOTICE records that it vendors the
  Sub-Store backend under apps/server/vendor/sub-store/).

  SubPilot reuses NO server-side code from SubPilot-Archive — the two have
  entirely different server architectures (SubPilot-Archive vendors Sub-Store
  and runs it on workerd; SubPilot implements its own
  storage/processing/distribution layer and delegates all format conversion to
  an external service).

  One file IS taken verbatim, as recorded in its own header comment:

      apps/web/src/utils/configPresets.js
          <- SubPilot-Archive: apps/server/src/subconv/presets.js

  The user-interface layout and interaction conventions are also aligned with
  SubPilot-Archive on purpose (the two are meant to feel like the same product
  family), but the Vue components are independently written, not copied.

SubConverter-Extended — external service, NO source code
--------------------------------------------------------
  Upstream:  https://github.com/Aethersailor/SubConverter-Extended
  License:   GNU General Public License v3.0

  SubPilot does not include any SubConverter source code. It talks to a
  SubConverter-Extended instance over HTTP (the `/sub` endpoint) at runtime.
  That backend is a separate deployment, supplied and operated by the user, and
  is not part of this distribution.

  The source-modifier syntax used when submitting multiple sources
  (`tag:name,provider:name,URL`) follows the convention established by the
  SubPilot-Archive / subweb frontends, for interoperability with the same
  backend.

Remote config preset data sources
---------------------------------
  The preset list in apps/web/src/utils/configPresets.js is a curated set of
  *URLs* pointing at remote configuration templates maintained by third
  parties. No template content is bundled — only the links are listed.

      Aethersailor/Custom_OpenClash_Rules   https://github.com/Aethersailor/Custom_OpenClash_Rules
      cmliu/sub-web-modify                  https://github.com/cmliu/sub-web-modify
      ACL4SSR/ACL4SSR                       https://github.com/ACL4SSR/ACL4SSR
      tindy2013/subconverter                https://github.com/tindy2013/subconverter
      SleepyHeeead/subconverter-config      https://github.com/SleepyHeeead/subconverter-config

  Credit for those templates belongs to their respective maintainers.

